      "text": "You lean over the broad copper vat resting in the dim Brineward dye shed. Its lip is thickly ringed with a pale crust, evidence of dried dye and minerals. The wool soaking within has stiffened, its fibers hardened and unyielding to the touch—an indication that the dyeing process halted prematurely or was fouled somehow. No obvious splashes or spills mar the area around the vat, and the shed itself holds no clear sign of disturbance or negligence. Whatever befell the wool occurred here, in silence."
